  "description": "A parametric FALSE CEILING on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nDROP IT ON A SPACE. It takes its extents from the host outline's bounding box, not from width and depth props, because a ceiling that could disagree with the room it sits in would be a second source of truth for the same rectangle. Margin insets it; Fit to host set to Exact stretches it back out.\n\nTWO LEVELS, AND THE COVE IS THE GAP BETWEEN THEM. A perimeter band at `bandSoffit` and a central panel at `panelSoffit`. The cove is never drawn as a thing — it is the reveal that exists because the panel sits higher than the band, and `coveReveal` reports it. Set the panel below the band and the metric goes to zero, which is the honest answer.\n\nTHE PANEL FILLS WHAT THE BANDS LEAVE. `_pu0 = _u0 + _bwC + _pin` — each edge is inset only by the band that is actually on that side, so dropping to Long sides or Three sides widens the panel automatically rather than leaving a gap.\n\nA SHADOW GAP IS AN INSET, NOT A SOLID. `_gapIn` simply adds to the panel inset on every banded side, so the gap and the panel cannot drift apart.\n\nTHE OPENING IS A SPLIT, NOT A SUBTRACTION. With `opening` on, the panel becomes four strips around the hole — left, right, below, above — because the quad-prism kernel extrudes plan quads and has no boolean. That is also why the hole is rectangular.\n\nDIMENSIONS AT THE DEFAULTS, on a 3.962 × 3.734 m room: band soffit 2.972, panel soffit 3.124, a 0.152 m cove reveal, 0.381 m of void above the band, 14.17 m of band run and 10.47 m² of panel.\n\nWHAT THIS CANNOT DO. The outline is the host's BOUNDING BOX — an L-shaped room gets a rectangular ceiling. There is no curved or chamfered cove profile: the kernel extrudes plan quads vertically, so Square, Stepped and Shadow gap are the three sections that can exist. Only one opening, and it is rectangular.",
